# The comms branch carries messages and nothing else.
#
# This branch is an orphan, so switching to it removes main's tracked files — including
# main's .gitignore. Everything left in the working tree (build output, node_modules, and
# critically `.env`) becomes untracked and therefore stageable. A careless `git add -A`
# here would commit secrets to a public repo.
#
# So: ignore everything, then allow back exactly the four things that belong.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!OPEN.md
!threads/
!threads/**
